    "All configurations remain candidates for the exact OpenCode harness until they pass compatibility admission.",
    "Public evidence from another harness supports candidacy but does not qualify an OpenCode configuration.",
    "Configured does not mean currently available; the Runner must perform live provider preflight.",
    "Automatic routes prefer capable OpenCode Go configurations, then admit Zen-only models when no Go configuration meets the requested capability, risk, or context.",
    "The console's Use balance option continues the same Go request against Zen credits after Go usage limits are reached; this is not a model-selection fallback.",
    "The runtime never switches models because of quota or provider failure. An exhausted Zen balance stops the run with ZEN_BALANCE_EXHAUSTED.",
    "2026-09-03: GPT 5.6 Sol was removed from Zen routing because the authenticated OpenAI provider already supplies it; the historical smoke remains documented outside this active registry.",
    "2026-09-03: DeepSeek V4 Flash on Go plus Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Haiku 4.5, Gemini 3.8 Flash, and Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite on Zen passed the sealed Builder smoke. Evidence tiers stay C or D; nothing is qualified.",
    "2026-09-03: admission is recorded per role under admission.roles; the catalog status can never be qualified. Only the certification process of the harness repository (certify.mjs) writes a qualified role entry, and the release check requires a complete qualified route before install or commit.",
    "2026-09-03: gpt-5.6-luna certified as goal-manager and planner and made primary for both; glm-5.3 stays qualified as the alternate but costs ~25x more per Goal (cache reads at 0.26/M and long explorations).",
    "2026-09-03: the nine OpenRouter configurations were removed from the registry. OpenRouter stays outside automatic routes by design (CODE_GENERATION_FLOW \u00a74) and none of them could ever be selected; the provider remains available in opencode.json for manual use only.",
    "2026-09-08: certification by fixture was removed. Admission is membership in a route (decided from public benchmarks) plus, per project, a fit check the first time a configuration is used and the metalog of real calls. The order inside a role is computed from price, cheapest first, per provider tier; a configuration with two failures in a row attributable to the model sinks to the bottom until it succeeds again. Catalog statuses are active, watch, deprecated.",
    "2026-09-08: the Planner and the Goal Manager may use the authenticated OpenAI provider as their first tier (user's subscription); the OpenAI configurations are added with the benchmark rebuild."
